This API prioritizes clarity, TypeScript type safety, and flexibility for seamless integration into your 3D applications.  We'll structure it around core animation concepts while allowing extensibility.

**1. Core Interfaces & Types:**

* **`CameraAnimationConfig`:**  Foundation of every animation.

   ```typescript
   interface CameraAnimationConfig {
     duration: number; // Animation length in milliseconds
     easing: EasingFunction; //  (linear, easeInQuad, easeOutCubic, etc.)
     targetCamera: CameraState; // Desired final camera state (defined below)
     interpolationMethod: InterpolationType; // 'linear', 'spline', 'custom' (allows for user-defined functions)
     onStart?: () => void; // Callback on animation start
     onProgress?: (progress: number) => void; //  Callback during animation
     onComplete?: () => void; // Callback on animation finish
   }

   type EasingFunction = (t: number) => number; // Custom easing functions encouraged!
   type InterpolationType = 'linear' | 'spline' | 'custom'; // Flexibility for interpolation techniques
   ```

* **`CameraState`:**  Precisely defines camera attributes.

   ```typescript
   interface CameraState {
     position: Vector3;
     rotation: Vector3; // Euler angles (x, y, z) or Quaternion representation (optional)
     fov: number; // Field of View (degrees)
     nearClip: number;
     farClip: number;
     //  ... additional camera settings (projection, aspectRatio, etc.) as needed
   }

   type Vector3 = [number, number, number]; //  Component-wise representation
