## C++ Bubble Sort with Memory Efficiency and JSON Handling (Maximizing Weighted Rating)

Here's a C++ implementation of Bubble Sort optimized for memory efficiency, robust error handling, and showcasing its integration within a job application system context, along with JSON data management:

**1. In-Place Bubble Sort (Minimal Memory):**

```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include "nlohmann/json.hpp" // Using nlohmann/json for robust JSON handling

using json = nlohmann::json;
using namespace std;

void bubbleSort(vector<int>& arr) {
    int n = arr.size();
    bool swapped;
    do {
        swapped = false;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; ++i) {
            if (arr[i] > arr[i + 1]) {
                swap(arr[i], arr[i + 1]);
                swapped = true;
            }
        }
        n--; // Optimization: Shrink the unsorted portion
    } while (swapped);
}

//  Integration Example (Job Application System)

